course: dictionary
lesson: 11641
title: Arranged: order and plans
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The books are arranged in alphabetical order on the shelf.» Arranged here means put in a certain order, so the books go A, B, C and so on. The words alphabetical order are the clue.
explain: Arranged can also mean planned. «Mum arranged a trip to the zoo for Saturday.» Mum did not put the trip in a row. She organised it ahead of time, so arranged means planned.
explain: In maths, arranged often means put into rows or groups. «The 24 chairs are arranged in 4 rows of 6.» Each row has 6 chairs, and 4 rows of 6 make 24 chairs altogether.
fact: Arranged means put in a certain order or pattern, such as in rows, by size or by colour.
fact: Arranged also means planned or organised, like an arranged meeting.
fact: A piece of music arranged for a band has been changed so those instruments can play it.
fact: «Arranged» is the past form of the verb arrange: arrange, arranges, arranged, arranging.
fact: Clue words like rows, order, size, colour or planned tell you which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «The cups were arranged in three rows of four.» How were the cups arranged? | Broken into pieces | Under the table | *In rows | In a messy pile
exercise: «The meeting was arranged for Tuesday at four o'clock.» What does arranged mean here? | *Planned | Painted | Broken | Lost
exercise: «The bottles are arranged from smallest to largest.» How are the bottles arranged? | Hidden in a box | At random, with no pattern | Upside down | *By size
test: «The books were arranged in alphabetical order.» What does arranged mean? | Thrown away | *Put in a certain order | Forgotten | Read aloud
test: Mum says, «I have arranged a party for your birthday.» What does arranged mean? | Shouted | Cancelled | Wrapped | *Planned
exam: Maths: «Ben arranged 15 counters into 3 equal rows.» How many counters are in each row? | 3 | *5 | 12 | 45
